<article class="env-remark" id="05N0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05N0">Remark <span data-tag="05N0">70.3.11</span>.</a> Here is an important special case of Proposition <a href="/tag/04AK" data-tag="04AK">70.3.10</a>. Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Then $X$ is locally of finite presentation over $S$ if and only if $X$, as a functor $(\mathit{Sch}/S)^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$, is limit preserving. Compare with Limits, Remark <a href="/tag/05LX" data-tag="05LX">32.6.2</a>. In fact, we will see in Lemma <a href="/tag/0CM6" data-tag="0CM6">70.3.12</a> below that it suffices if the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits X(T_ i) \longrightarrow X(T)  \]
</div>
  <p> is surjective whenever $T = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i$ is a directed limit of affine schemes over $S$. </p>
</article>